Host port of EE-GCC 2.9-ee-991111-01 (GirianSeed/ee-gcc src.tar.gz + Sony's sce-patch) to 64-bit macOS,
built with Apple clang, for arm64 and x86_64. Apply with `patch -p1` in src/, then copy xm-darwin.h to
gcc/config/. What each part is for:

1. config.sub, gcc/config.sub, gcc/configure: accept aarch64/x86_64-apple-darwin hosts (xm-darwin.h).
2. libiberty/strerror.c: hide the SDK's `const int sys_nerr` like sys_errlist. include/obstack.h: no lvalue
   casts (modern C rejects them; same expansion otherwise).
3. gcc/expr.h, gcc/expr.c: the generated gen_* functions are K&R (non-variadic) but were called through
   `rtx (*)(rtx, ...)`. On Apple arm64 variadic arguments go on the stack, so the operands arrived as garbage
   (cc1 crashed on `return a + b;`). Unprototyped pointers, as genoutput.c itself declares the table.
4. LONG32: `long' is 32 bits on the original i386 host and 64 here. HOST_WIDE_INT is `long long' on both (the
   r5900 target forces it) and float folding is software (REAL_ARITHMETIC), so only these differ:
   - gcc/real.c endian(): 32-bit target words are returned sign-extended, as a 32-bit `long' holds them. The
     original therefore folds `union { double d; long long l; } u; u.d = 1.1; return u.l;` to
     0xffffffff9999999a (its operand_subword ORs in the sign-extended low word); this reproduces that.
   - gcc/config/mips/mips.c: the words (and a large-frame offset) are printed as 32-bit values again.
   - gcc/dbxout.c: stabs type ranges switch to octal at gdb's 32-bit `long' (`int:t1=r1;0000...;').
5. Three latent bugs found with AddressSanitizer, each reading or writing past an object, so their effect
   depended on the host's memory layout:
   - gcc/haifa-sched.c init_rgn_data_dependences(): the int array bb_pending_lists_length was cleared with
     n * sizeof (rtx), i.e. n * 8 bytes here and past the end of its alloca; n * 4 on the original.
   - gcc/jump.c delete_barrier_successors(): SET_SRC/SET_DEST of a jump's pattern were read without checking
     that the pattern is a SET (a RETURN or ADDR_VEC has fewer operands, so the next object was read).
   - gcc/loop.c find_and_verify_loops(): a LOOP_CONT note outside any loop was stored at
     loop_number_loop_cont[-1]. In the original's packed alloca blocks (n * 4 bytes each, seen in its
     disassembly) that is loop_number_cont_dominator[max_loop_num - 1]; it is stored there now.
6. The C++ front end (cc1plus):
   - gcc/cp/cp-tree.h, gcc/cp/errfn.c, gcc/cp/typeck2.c: cp_error, cp_warning, cp_pedwarn and the rest are
     variadic, but cp-tree.h declared them `()', so all 826 calls passed their arguments in registers while
     the callee read them from the stack (most diagnostics crashed cc1plus). They are prototyped now. errfn.c
     calls error, warning, pedwarn and their _with_file_and_line forms (variadic) and compiler_error (K&R)
     through one unprototyped pointer: each is now called the way it is defined. typeck2.c's readonly_error
     kept cp_error/cp_pedwarn in an unprototyped pointer.
   - gcc/cp/decl.c grokdeclarator(): `next = &name' pointed at a block-local variable that the loop read
     after the block had ended (found by AddressSanitizer). The original's stack slot still held it.
   - gcc/cp/call.c add_function_candidate(): CONVS was uninitialised on the not-viable path. Clang treats
     passing an uninitialised value as undefined and deleted that path, so non-viable candidates became
     viable (`foo f;' was ambiguous with the copy constructor).
   - gcc/cp/cp-tree.h IS_SIGNATURE: a pointer to member function type keeps its RECORD_TYPE in
     TYPE_LANG_SPECIFIC, and IS_SIGNATURE read a struct lang_type bit from that tree: the low byte of its
     (null) TREE_TYPE on the original, part of a TREE_CHAIN address on a 64-bit host, which made
     `(int (A::*)()) 0' a "signature type" on x86_64. Only class types are checked now.
   - gcc/cp/rtti.c build_x_typeid(): NONNULL was uninitialised, and only ever set to 1. In the original it
     was never 0 in any test, so `typeid (*p)' got no null check; it starts at 1 now instead of holding
     whatever the port's stack has (0 adds a call to __throw_bad_typeid).
   - gcc/cp/decl2.c, gcc/cp/pt.c, gcc/cp/typeck.c: the order of evaluation of call arguments. The original
     was built with GCC 2.7.2 on i386, which evaluates them right to left; clang goes left to right. Where
     two arguments instantiate templates (build_expr_from_tree, tsubst_copy, tsubst_expr) or may synthesize
     methods and give diagnostics (rationalize_conditional_expr, build_component_ref, build_modify_expr),
     the later arguments are computed first, so templates are instantiated, and their functions output, in
     the original's order (g++.pt/sizeof.C: bar<15> before bar<8>).
   - LONG32 again: cp/typeck.c and c-typeck.c (the -Wsign-compare "promoted ~unsigned" check stops at a
     32-bit `long'), cp/typeck2.c (an enum value printed through a 32-bit `long'), cp/error.c (a 128-bit
     constant printed with "%x%08x" and two 64-bit words: i386 printed the two halves of the high word).
7. gcc/except.c, exception handling (shared with C -fexceptions):
   - remove_handler() compared handler labels by pointer, also for regions of functions already compiled,
     whose labels' memory has been freed and reused: a new label at the same address removed an unrelated
     handler and its exception table entry. Where that happens depends on the host's object sizes, so it
     compares the (unique) label numbers now.
   - get_first_handler() read function_eh_regions[-1] for a region it couldn't find. On the original that
     is the malloc chunk header, and following it crashed the compiler with SIGSEGV. It raises SIGSEGV now,
     so the messages are the same (cc1plus's "Internal compiler error.", or the driver's for cc1).
8. gcc/sibcall.c optimize_sibling_and_tail_recursive_calls() called find_basic_blocks with 3 of its 4
   arguments (it is undeclared there), so DO_CLEANUP was whatever lay in its place: in the port, a register
   left over from jump_optimize_minimal, 0 or not depending on how jump.c was compiled (x86_64 kept dead
   inlined loops: c-torture 960209-1.c at -O3). On the original it was INSNS, still on the stack from the
   call before (GCC defers the pop), so never 0. It passes 1.
9. gcc/tree.c append_random_chars(): a C++ file that defines no global object names its EH frame function
   and anonymous namespaces after the file plus 6 characters from the time of day and the pid, so the
   original never gives the same object twice. The port adds 0 instead, which is what the original adds
   when tools/fixed-clock.so is preloaded (its gettimeofday returns tv_sec = pid, tv_usec = 0). With that
   the original is reproducible too, and both give the same names.
10. Found by comparing the -da dumps with the original's:
   - Argument order (see 6) in the back end, where one argument can make a pseudo or emit an insn before
     another: gcc/expr.c emit_move_insn_1 (complex moves; g++.brendan complex1.C's RTL numbered the two
     addresses the other way round), expand_expr (complex conjugate, highpart multiply),
     expand_builtin_apply_args, do_jump_by_parts_equality; gcc/optabs.c expand_binop,
     expand_twoval_binop; gcc/function.c assign_parms; gcc/integrate.c copy_rtx_and_substitute (inlined
     calls); gcc/config/mips/mips.c expand_block_move; gcc/config/mips/mips.md mulsi3, mulsidi3,
     umulsidi3 (three gen_reg_rtx in one argument list); gcc/combine.c simplify_and_const_int;
     gcc/c-common.c truthvalue_conversion.
   - gcc/haifa-sched.c get_visual_tbl_length(): "  %33s" wrote 36 bytes into alloca (35); the original's
     alloca rounded to 36, the port's fortified sprintf aborted every -da compile that scheduled.
     print_value() printed CONST_DOUBLE words through a 32-bit `long' (LONG32).
11. Error recovery of rejected code, so the messages are the same:
   - gcc/cp/decl.c init_decl_processing(): error recovery reads fields that an ERROR_MARK node lacks. On the
     original the 12-byte error_mark_node was followed by error_mark_list and this_identifier, so those
     reads found their fields; here they found other nodes' fields. error_mark_node now has room for every
     field, holding what the original read in those that g++ tests reach: TREE_OPERAND 0 is
     error_mark_node (build_new_1 after a failed operator new: g++.jason/dtor3.C and 6 more), DECL_CONTEXT
     is 4 (g++.brendan/crash8.C and 3 more crash on it), TYPE_NONCOPIED_PARTS and DECL_LANG_SPECIFIC are 0.
   - gcc/tree.c make_node(): error recovery also reads other nodes' fields from identifiers, which on the
     original found the identifier's name and the nodes after it: TYPE_MAIN_VARIANT was 0 (g++.pt/crash1.C),
     DECL_LANG_SPECIFIC 1 (g++.pt/friend37.C), and both crashed. Identifiers now have room for every field,
     all 0, which crashes the same way.
   - gcc/integrate.c expand_inline_function(): after errors DECL_RESULT can be null; the original loaded
     DECL_RTL from it before testing for a void function and crashed, clang moved the load to where it is
     used. It is a volatile load now (g++.law/inline2.C at -O2).
   - gcc/toplev.c: cc1 dies of SIGSEGV when it gets SIGBUS, which macOS raises for some bad accesses that
     i386 Linux reports as SIGSEGV; the driver prints the number (c-torture 950922-1.c).
12. abort () prints __FILE__ and __LINE__. So that its messages name the original's lines, a `#line N'
   follows each change above that adds or removes lines in a file that calls abort (), and the mips.md
   changes (copied into insn-emit.c) keep their line counts. (build.sh builds in src/obj, as the original
   was built, so __FILE__ is ../../gcc/expr.c.)
